Guidance for agents and human contributors working in {{ .name }}.

## Conventions

- Build with Bazel; the dev environment is hermetic (pinned toolchains,
  direnv-activated) — never install tools globally.
- The dbt project lives in `dbt/` and mirrors the target database's schema
  layout: `models/model/` (core models → schema `model`), `models/expose/`
  (analysis-ready marts → schema `expose`), `models/semantic/` (governed
  views → schema `semantic`).
- Run dbt through the project verbs (`gup dbt build`, `gup dbt test`) so the
  Bazel-pinned engine is used; never install dbt globally.
- SQL style is enforced by sqlfluff and Python by ruff (`gup lint` /
  `gup format`); keep both green before committing.
